  "thumbnailAlt": "Hotel Booking Request form beside a photo of guests checking in at a hotel reception desk",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A hotel booking request form is a form that collects a guest's check-in and check-out dates, number of adults and children, preferred room type and special requests so the front desk can check availability and send back a confirmed rate. Because nothing is charged at this step, this template suits small hotels, guest houses and B&Bs that confirm every booking by hand, and it captures arrival time and occasions so you can prepare the room.",
    "audience": "Independent hotels, B&Bs, guest houses, inns, hostels, homestays and holiday-let owners who confirm reservations personally.",
    "useCases": [
      "A Book Now button on a small hotel website without a booking engine",
      "Group and wedding room blocks where each guest sends their own request",
      "Direct bookings from returning guests to avoid online travel agency fees",
      "Off-season or long-stay requests that need a custom rate"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Turn on the email plugin's copy to the respondent so guests get a record of exactly what they asked for.",
      "Embed the form on your rooms page and add your logo and a lobby photo so it looks like part of your site.",
      "Use response limits or a close date to stop requests for a fully booked festival weekend."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a hotel booking request form include?",
        "answer": "Guest name, email and phone, check-in and check-out dates, number of adults and children, number of rooms, room type and bed preference, estimated arrival time, purpose or occasion of the stay, special requests such as accessibility or cots, and a note that the request is not confirmed until the hotel replies."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is a booking request the same as a confirmed reservation?",
        "answer": "No. A request asks for the room; the booking is confirmed only when the hotel replies with availability, rate and its deposit and cancellation terms. Say this clearly on the form to avoid no-shows and disputes."
      },
      {
        "question": "How should I take a deposit for a request?",
        "answer": "This form does not take money. After you confirm availability, send the guest your usual secure link or ask them to call with card details, following your bank's guidance."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use this for group or wedding room blocks?",
        "answer": "Yes. Share one link with the group and each guest submits their own dates and room type, so your reservations team can match them to the block."
      }
    ]
  },
